From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: our own Welcome Tour

ChromeOS's Welcome Tour never ran on NickelOS (it needs Google Sync to
say the account is new) and was Google's: it ended in the Explore app,
which NickelOS does not have. Now it is NickelOS's, on ChromeOS's own
tour machinery (the dimmed screen, help bubbles on the launcher's apps,
Next and Back):

1. the shelf, 2. the launcher, 3. search, 4. Files (My files is the Linux
home; cloud storage shows up there), 5. Bazaar (Linux apps from Flathub),
6. the Terminal (a real shell with sudo; Gentoo underneath, eix
and emerge), 7. Settings. Its last button,
"Open the NickelOS guide", opens nickelos.dev/help in the browser; saying
no thanks opens nothing.

Who gets it: each user once, until they finish it or say no thanks, in
the Chrome that runs as their own Linux user (a sign-in starts in the
login screen's Chrome, run as chronos: Chrome 0008), instead of Google
Sync's "first sync ever". Bazaar and the Terminal get element identifiers
in the launcher (kNickelBazaarAppElementId, kNickelTerminalAppElementId).
Their help bubble ids and metrics steps are the Explore app's and the
status area's, which this tour has no steps for.

